  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"We asked 12...homeless men for their footprints... They took off their shoes...touched the shining copper plates...leaving an impression"--Leaf [4].</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Bound in parchment; in slipcase.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"This book was designed and printed by Jacob Samuel. The plates were made by the artist in Santa Monica, California in April, 2003 using hard and soft ground etching techniques. The papers are natural Gampi and Rives de Lin. The printing assistant was Eric Ziemann. The text was edited by C.A. Samuel. Typography and letterpress by Les Ferriss. Bookbinding and boxes by Klaus-Ullrich S. Rötzscher. The edition is limited to twenty numbered copies: 1-6 are bound books; 7-20 are loose portfolios. There are three sets of artist's proofs"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
